  "reproduction": "Start Monster Hunt from the actual lobby, choose Apocalypse/Morgas, dodge, finish the battle, acknowledge the result, then enter the same target again in the same document. The legacy trio cache retained the resolved pose atlas after Pixi unloaded the first encounter. The second fight had valid object bounds and alpha but zero opaque pixels in all four skill poses. The left-facing authored idle art was mirrored a second time by the enemy view.",
  "fix": "Use the live Pixi asset cache on each load. Restore the loaded idle texture, authored dimensions, visible body and facing before recording a neutral pose. If the pose atlas cannot decode, keep the idle body and play the remaining effects through the authoritative impact. Normalize both formation and single-boss entries.",
  "fixture": "An isolated server-generated battle uses the five card identities from the report, Helios King, Bikini Joeun, and a Z-body. Gear, power, equipment and seed are controlled test inputs. After the six escorts fall Morgas reaches 14.37% HP. A separate historical battle with other mercenaries exercises the mobile and host paths. Production APIs were intercepted into an isolated local fixture.",
  "method": "Frame samples check direction against the allied formation, body visibility/scales/screen bounds, and opaque pixels in the decoded source at 64 px. Candidate and published party checks additionally draw each actual pose as a Pixi sprite in an offscreen render target and read its opaque pixels. Screenshots show the on-stage body. Milliseconds from the fight button pointerdown to the first selectable safe-zone frame. Frame intervals are browser RAF samples, not display refresh-rate promises. Isolated Windows host and touch-emulated WebKit/H5; no physical phone.",
  "performanceNotes": "The controlled WebKit 390px entry-only comparison starts in a fresh browser context, then repeats the same opponent after the normal result dialog. It uses the same isolated party and ends the challenge on an unsafe zone after measuring input readiness. Full fights use the safe zone. First/repeat times were 6697/2837 ms before and 5612/2388 ms after in this single pair. The local fight response took 16–22 ms. Emulated WebKit produced long frames in both full-fight runs; example p95 45/45 ms before and 56/62 ms after on the alternate party, with overlapping host build work on the latter. The reported party on desktop stayed at 4 ms p95. These measurements do not establish physical iPhone performance. Releasing expired GPU images and letting Pixi reuse living assets avoids retaining the previous encounter’s bitmaps without adding a per-frame update.",
